Z||000002||loafer87gt||10-11-2001||07:52 PM||||Yeah, I have USAF, Janes f18, WWII fighters, and Longbow Gold. I loved USAF, but had to quit playing it after upgrading my computer as the radar display and the right MFD no longer displayed on my GeForce card. I was happy to hear that XIcat software will be releasing Janes Attack Squadron. It was cancelled last year because of funding, but it is now in the works again. It looks to be a really good simulation of the WWII front. Aside from the Janes games, I LOVE falcon 4.0. With the latest realism patch I downloaded, there is over 50 steps to just get your engines started. I feel pretty confident after playing through that sim that I could manage my way around in a real F-16. LOL. Also, be sure to grab the demo for IL-2 Stormovik. The graphics are unbelievable, and it is supposed to be the next big thing in the sim world. ||||reg||1
